{"name":"Haute Couture","hex":"#a0252a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"haute couture","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["High fashion as produced in Paris and imitated in other fashion capitals such as New York, London, and Milan.","The fashion houses or fashion designers that create exclusive and often trendsetting fashions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haute_couture"}],"entries":[{"title":"Haute couture","blocks":[{"text":"Haute couture is the creation of exclusive custom-fitted high-end fashion design. The term haute couture generally refers to a specific type of upper garment common in Europe during the 16th to the 18th century or to the upper portion of a modern dress to distinguish it from the skirt and sleeves. Beginning in the mid-nineteenth century, Paris became the centre of a growing industry that focused on making outfits from high-quality, expensive, and often unusual fabric, sewn with extreme attention to detail and finished by the most experienced and capable of sewers, often using time-consuming, hand-executed techniques. Couture is also commonly used on its own as an abbreviation of haute couture, referring to the same concept in spirit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Pierre_Balmain_and_Ruth_Ford%2C_photographed_by_Carl_Van_Vechten%2C_November_9%2C_1947.jpg/330px-Pierre_Balmain_and_Ruth_Ford%2C_photographed_by_Carl_Van_Vechten%2C_November_9%2C_1947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haute_couture","wikidata":"Q216053"},{"title":"Haute Couture (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Haute Couture is the second extended play by MiSaMo, a sub-unit of girl group Twice. It was released by Warner Music Japan on November 6, 2024. The EP contains seven tracks, including the lead single, \"Identity\", and \"New Look\", a cover of Namie Amuro's song of the same name. Each member of MiSaMo also has a solo song, available as bonus tracks on some editions of the EP."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a1/MiSaMo_Haute_Couture_cover_art.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haute_Couture_(EP)","wikidata":"Q131007827"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_MET.jpg/500px-The_MET.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_MET.jpg/1280px-The_MET.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_MET.jpg/500px-The_MET.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The annual Met Gala, held at the Metropolitan Museum of Art on the Upper East Side of Manhattan and organized by Vogue high-fashion magazine, hosts the largest haute couture fashion night annually.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_MET.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg/500px-Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg/500px-Carolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haute couture fashion models walk the runway during New York Fashion Week.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarolina_Herrera_AW14_12.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Chanel_Haute_Couture_Fall-Winter_2011.jpg/500px-Chanel_Haute_Couture_Fall-Winter_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Chanel_Haute_Couture_Fall-Winter_2011.jpg/500px-Chan